course: dictionary
lesson: 10723
title: Unwritten words and rules
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unwritten means not written down. Something unwritten lives in speech or memory, passed from person to person by talking and doing. The prefix un- often means "not", so unwritten means "not written".
explain: «Autistic people may find unwritten playground rules confusing, and a patient buddy can help.» These rules are not on a sign or in a list. Nobody wrote them down, so you have to notice what others do. The word unwritten tells you that clue straight away.
explain: Unwritten can also mean not yet written. A blank page waiting for a story is an unwritten page. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: does "not written down" still make sense? If it does, you have understood the word.
fact: Unwritten means not written down; it exists only in speech or memory.
fact: An «unwritten rule» is one that everybody follows or knows, even though nobody wrote it down.
fact: The UK has an «unwritten constitution», which means it is not one single document.
fact: Some languages are unwritten, so they are passed on by speaking rather than by writing.
fact: Unwritten can also mean not yet written, like an unwritten chapter.
exercise: «Autistic people may find unwritten playground rules confusing.» What does unwritten mean here? | Written on a big sign | Lost forever | Very long and difficult | *Not written down, but known or followed
exercise: Which is an example of an unwritten rule? | *Queuing politely without anyone telling you to | A sign that says NO RUNNING | A law written in a numbered book | A rule printed on the school gate
exercise: Some languages are unwritten. How are they passed on? | By sending emails | By writing them in books | *By speaking them from person to person | By painting them on walls only
test: An unwritten story means a story that is: | *Not yet written down | Finished and printed | Written in green ink | Read out loud by a teacher
test: The UK constitution is called unwritten because it: | Is only one page long | *Is not one single document | Is written in gold | Has no words at all
exam: The prefix un- means not, so what does unwritten mean? | Written twice | Read silently | Written in pencil | *Not written down
